      "writtenOn": "2023-11-16T10:02:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The implementations of this trait look to mostly be using `\u0026args[n]`, so this is probably better as `\u0026[Value]`.  That would also allow use of `\u0026req[1..]` rather than `req.remove(0)` in `deserialize_from_packet()`.",
      "revId": "daa6444d2605e8248d3559347da519fb34f69839",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3148c547_5c37095d",
        "filename": "secretkeeper/comm/src/data_types/request.rs",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1897307
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-17T18:35:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Implementation of this trait for other request types like StoreSecret would need the args to be passed by value [otherwise there will be multiple clones of values]. GetVersion is a rather simple example with empty args. \nTo have a look at how other requets implements this trait, see WIP patch \n\nhttps://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/2833051/1/secretkeeper/comm/src/data_types/request_response_impl.rs",
      "parentUuid": "ce5e964e_ba26877a",
      "revId": "daa6444d2605e8248d3559347da519fb34f69839",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "82eaf6d1_ef92b49a",
        "filename": "secretkeeper/comm/src/data_types/request.rs",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 43,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836235
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-16T10:02:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The combination of `\u0026self` and returning a `Vec` forces the implementation to allocate in all circumstances -- maybe either consume (`fn args(self) -\u003e Vec\u003cValue\u003e`) or return a reference (`fn args(\u0026self) -\u003e \u0026[Value]`) and let the caller decide if they need to clone or not.",
      "revId": "daa6444d2605e8248d3559347da519fb34f69839",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e90088c9_aebfb07b",
        "filename": "secretkeeper/comm/src/data_types/request.rs",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 43,
      "author": {
        "id": 1897307
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-17T18:35:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Option1:\nI actually do want args \u0026 serialize_to_packet to consume Self. Unfortunately, Consuming Self will leads to unsized param \u0026 this is not stable yet - https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/48055\n\nOption2:\nfn args(\u0026self) -\u003e \u0026[Value]). The implementation of the trait can maintain \narguments in whatever form they like, it doesn\u0027t have to be vector. For ex, \n\n```\npub struct StoreSecretRequest {\n    // Unique identifier of the secret\n    id: Id,\n    // The secret the client wishes to store\n    secret: Secret,\n    // The dice policy corresponding to the secret\n    sealing_policy: Vec\u003cu8\u003e,\n}\n```\n\nSo I\u0027m not sure if returning a slice of Values in such cases is possible at all",
      "parentUuid": "82eaf6d1_ef92b49a",
      "revId": "daa6444d2605e8248d3559347da519fb34f69839",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
